1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his trial, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
A young Yami was out training when he received a request to protect a village from a group of bandit mages.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
But before he knew it, he found himself outnumbered and surrounded.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
And during that fateful fight...

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Yami, I believe your name was. Watch my back if you wouldn't mind.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Yami met William Von Gens, who was on his own mission nearby.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:57,000
I intend to become the captain of the Magic Knight Squad. Then it's a contest. Let's see who gets there first.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:05,000
After all that, a whole bunch of stuff happened. Years went by. Old Julius was crowned as the Wizard King.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,000
And as for me and my new pal Goldiguts, both of us ended up getting promoted to vice-captain of the Grey Deer.

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Then one day...

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Ah, yes. It's wonderful to see you. How are things?

14
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Let's skip the small talk if you don't mind. I agree.

15
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,000
By the way, William, I was happy to hear about your excellent work investigating the dungeon that was recently discovered.

16
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Oh, that was nothing, sir.

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Don't be so modest. You valiantly used your magic to rescue your trapped squadmates.

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Boy, I wish I could have seen that!

19
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Ah, and such a noble effort is obviously worthy of a star. Nice work.

20
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
I'm honored. Thank you, Your Majesty.

21
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
And apparently you fought like a man possessed during the treacherous battle to defend the village of Kuka.

22
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Correct me if I'm wrong, but I believe I heard you slice the enemy's giant stone magic warrior in two.

23
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Oh, come on. That was amazing. And I'm gonna get a star for my heroics too, right?

24
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Of course! Your captain must be beaming with pride right now.

25
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Wizard King, it's time, sir.

26
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Right, I almost forgot. I appreciate you coming all this way when you're so busy, but…

27
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,000
But…

28
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,000
It would appear that I have a new assignment lined up for you to do.

29
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Bandits?

30
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Indeed. They've been making mischief all over. Do you think you could take care of them for us?

31
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Certainly. We are magic knights, after all. We are here to serve the people of the Clover Kingdom. So we'll go.

32
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
And happily. However…

33
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Why are you sending us and only us?

34
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Well, we have reason to believe that these bandits may be receiving help from someone who's part of the magic knights.

35
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Ah, so it'll take a little finesse.

36
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Hmm. This isn't just some ordinary band of miscreants. From what we've observed, we understand these people are considerably powerful,

37
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
their leadership is unusually strong, and they're currently in possession of ancient magic items. Plus…

38
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:06,000
It seems they may have absconded with some magic artifacts that were found in the dungeons.

39
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
So you came to us. Well, I guess that makes sense.

40
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:17,000
If you'd addressed the magic knights as a whole, someone within the ranks could have disposed of evidence that might reveal the truth. That's why we need to handle it discreetly.

41
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
That about covers it.

42
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Just one thing though, Julius. What are you gonna do if it turns out William and I were the big traitors all along? We would probably turn a blind eye to those bandits, right?

43
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Indeed, that would be a problem. But then… I like to believe I know you fellows fairly well. Even from the days before you became members of the magic knights. So I'm assuming it's safe to trust you. Although if you do decide to betray me, I guess that's the way life goes.

44
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Huh. You got a strange outlook on life, Julius.

45
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Marks, would you please do the honors?

46
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Yes, sir.

47
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,000
The towns and villages that have been attacked by the bandits are indicated here.

48
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Oh, I see. They're all over the place. They must not want us to figure out which area they're gonna go after next. Huh.

49
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:11,000
We've sent word to local magic knight squads telling them to be extra vigilant. But even that bit of information could be subject to leaks.

50
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
They tend to focus on the places with weaker defenses.

51
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:21,000
So basically, we're gonna have to guess at what their next target will be and hope we get it right. And that will not be an easy task.

52
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
No, I think it will be. Huh?

53
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:37,000
We can start by ruling out all the spots that have already been hit. The places that are most at risk would be where treasure has recently been discovered. Or anywhere a harvest is about to take place. Especially a large one.

54
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,000
That's real nice detective work, but we're still looking at one or two dozen here.

55
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:49,000
We can exclude any location that's near a place they've already attacked as well. And they'll most likely avoid any areas that are on high alert.

56
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Maybe, but...

57
00:04:50,000 --> 00:05:04,000
But that's too many for just the two of us to manage. I'm well aware. So, here and here. This village as well. Could you dispatch some squads to these three areas to watch for bandits?

58
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:09,000
What for? If word gets out, it'll be all for nothing anyway, you know?

59
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:14,000
That's brilliant. And assuming the information does get leaked, we can simply use it to our advantage.

60
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Correct. It's safe to assume the bandits will avoid the regions where Magic Knights are. They're probably going to appear where they believe no one will be waiting for them.

61
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Yeah, obviously I knew that. I was just making sure you knew it too, that's all.

62
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Anyway, it looks like we've narrowed it down to one of two spots. The town of Aimaya or Zokudani Village.

63
00:05:36,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Kikiiki, kiki, kibibimeno koto. W**ła, wa, wa, wa wa Joel kano ygada data kafawa bwoバ bwokokok

64
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:32,980
Thank you.

65
00:06:33,000 --> 00:07:02,980
Thank you.

66
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Thank you.

67
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:41,600
Exactly. If the bandits show up in Sokodani looking for that treasure, then they would have received their intel far too quickly. In which case there's no doubt we have a traitor in our midst.

68
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,960
Got it. How's I, Maya?

69
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:44,060
Yeah.

70
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:53,320
It seems to be all clear as well. They're done reaping and now they're preparing for their harvest festival. It's sure to be a plentiful crop this year.

71
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:56,440
Well, that'll give the bandits something to steal.

72
00:07:58,140 --> 00:08:08,480
Look, just so we're on the same page. No matter which of us sees the thieves first, we shouldn't do it alone. We should contact each other and wait to attack until we're both present. Agreed?

73
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:14,680
Yeah, yeah. But you better not pull a fast one on me and try and get all the stars for yourself.

74
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:20,140
I'd never. Anyway, I'll let you know if I notice any movement.

75
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:33,380
Guess it's that time.

76
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:38,740
Hey, Mass Boy. You're on the move. You there? Hey!

77
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:43,420
The hell? It was working fine earlier.

78
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:49,480
There's something about this key. Are those guys blocking the flow of mana somehow?

79
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:53,380
They gotta be doing something to break up our lines of communication.

80
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:56,280
These are not your run-of-the-mill bandits.

81
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:02,700
That means there is a traitor. And we just have to figure out who.

82
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:08,420
Looks like about 30 of them. No more than that. I'm gonna say it's around 50.

83
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:15,560
50. No matter which of us sees the thieves first, we shouldn't do it alone. We should contact each other.

84
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:19,740
Well, we can't contact each other, so I'm moving on to plan B.

85
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,560
Sorry, I'm going solo.

86
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:29,060
Stop them before they get there.

87
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,860
Dark Cloak.

88
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:35,900
Black Blade!

89
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:39,740
Who's back there?

90
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,640
Spread out! We've been spotted!

91
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:47,960
Who is this guy?

92
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:51,380
A magic knight? You've got guts fighting us all alone.

93
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:52,940
Yeah, big mistake, pal.

94
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:56,660
Whatever. Dark magic. Dark Cloak.

95
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:58,400
Lightless Flash!

96
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,120
Yeah!

97
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:02,900
I got about half of them.

98
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:20,240
You must be the boss man.

99
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:23,680
Wait, I think I know you.

100
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:26,320
That's odd. You don't look like a magic knight.

101
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:29,260
Hey, I recognize you.

102
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,300
Yeah, you're gonna have to remind me.

103
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:36,480
Years ago, you were the one who interfered with our attack on that pathetic village.

104
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:39,180
Who knew I'd get to settle a score here?

105
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:40,820
I don't follow.

106
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:46,460
Oh, that was you.

107
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:48,180
I remember now.

108
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:52,460
He looks flashy, but he actually doesn't have a whole lot of magic power to speak of.

109
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,920
That wand he's got's another story, though.

110
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:58,940
I bet you anything it's a priceless treasure that was dug up in one of those dungeons.

111
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:02,280
I've changed quite a bit since the last time we fought.

112
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:02,920
Who cares?

113
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:05,140
I'm more interested in who gave you that wand.

114
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:07,800
You want to find out, you'll have to beat me first.

115
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:13,540
It's over!

116
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:26,160
That turned out to be a whole lot of nothing.

117
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:28,020
Now.

118
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,000
Speak up.

119
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:31,760
And I want every single detail.

120
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:34,560
Who was it that gave you this fancy magic wand?

121
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:38,040
Five seconds.

122
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:39,480
And now four.

123
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:41,200
Okay, okay, I'll tell you.

124
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,760
The truth is...

125
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:47,520
Get back inside!

126
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:50,780
That's it!

127
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:52,440
Don't you move, Mr. Magic Knight!

128
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:54,700
Take one step,

129
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:56,840
and the old lady dies.

130
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:59,760
Then you're gonna suffer a hundred times worse.

131
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,080
What does that mean?

132
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:04,680
Your little buddies won't do any more good than they did last time we fought.

133
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:07,360
No, you're obviously capable of defeating my men.

134
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:08,560
But this?

135
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:17,800
What the...

136
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:21,200
That's an earth magic spell by the name of Witch Hunter Claus.

137
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:23,000
Impressive, isn't it?

138
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,640
Then that's not all.

139
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:29,440
You're also trapped by a binding spell called Sheephorn Snag.

140
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,040
Wait a sec.

141
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:30,800
Wait a sec.

142
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,240
Don't I know you two?

143
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,100
That's right.

144
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:37,020
Crimson Goat and Silver Mole.

145
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:39,920
I never thought there'd be two traitors among us.

146
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:45,480
You guys have been feeding those bandits intel and magic items so they would go out and attack the villages and towns.

147
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:46,720
Haven't you?

148
00:12:46,720 --> 00:12:48,940
That won't help you.

149
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:52,080
You can't break those bonds with mortal strength.

150
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:56,800
You're a damn disgrace to magic knights everywhere.

151
00:12:57,800 --> 00:12:58,880
Ah, I remember.

152
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:02,160
You're that foreigner the Wizard King just promoted, aren't you?

153
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:03,460
Yami Sukuhiro.

154
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:06,020
I suspected he might be plotting something.

155
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:08,280
I guess this means I was correct.

156
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:13,260
In other words, when the Wizard King ordered the magic knights to guard these areas against bandit invasions,

157
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:17,360
it was nothing but a simple diversion, an attempt to narrow down where we'd strike next.

158
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:19,760
And you fell for it hook, line, and sinker.

159
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,460
I have to say, the whole situation's terribly amusing.

160
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:23,380
Excellent.

161
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:25,900
You two managed to capture him just in the nick of time.

162
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:28,160
I should have known you would have no problems with traps.

163
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:30,340
Stop standing around and go look for that treasure.

164
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:31,460
Oh, right.

165
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:32,180
Of course.

166
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:34,020
I'll have a look around the chief's house.

167
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,780
You, take me there.

168
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:36,840
Oh, okay.

169
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,520
Give me a hand, boys.

170
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:39,260
Yes, sir.

171
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:45,340
The magic knights are supposed to protect the people, not ransack their towns.

172
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:47,360
You're both monsters.

173
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:53,900
We'll be certain to fulfill our duty as magic knights by making the Wizard King aware that there's been a bandit incident in this area.

174
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:56,500
Don't go thinking you'll finish me off that easily.

175
00:13:56,820 --> 00:13:58,500
I'll pay you back times a million.

176
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:00,440
Oh, I'm shaking in my shoe.

177
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:02,540
Anyway, we're done here.

178
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:10,160
How much longer can you keep that up?

179
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:12,100
You might as well surrender already.

180
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,500
Nah, it'll take a whole lot more than this.

181
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:16,240
I'm not done.

182
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:18,160
I'll break through.

183
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:21,120
Surely you've exhausted all your strength by now.

184
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:22,760
I'm just getting started.

185
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:26,220
I'll reach my limit and push past it.

186
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:29,260
Here and now.

187
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:42,380
Dracaena Formation.

188
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:53,600
Are you all right?

189
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:54,660
About time.

190
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,640
I got here as quickly as I could.

191
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:58,680
I realized we've been cut off.

192
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:03,460
And then, well, the only logical assumption was that the bandits must have appeared in Zokodane.

193
00:15:04,660 --> 00:15:05,200
Uh-huh.

194
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:07,300
Guess I owe you one then.

195
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:09,960
In fact, I'll pay it off right now.

196
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:11,260
Ready for this?

197
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:13,620
Those punks are the traitors.

198
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:15,480
Gotenmo, you say?

199
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:16,920
Good to know.

200
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:18,840
Ah, William Vangeans.

201
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:22,340
I take it you're acting under the Wizard King's orders as well.

202
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:26,120
Then we'll just eliminate you and Yamae Sukuhiro in one fell swoop.

203
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:33,420
This again?

204
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:42,640
Now, attack of the horn!

205
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:50,000
Dark cloak like the slag!

206
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:58,640
I believe I said I'd pay you back a million times over, didn't I?

207
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:02,220
Um, please go easy on me if you don't mind.

208
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:09,500
Not bad at all, if you ask me.

209
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:12,280
Let me suggest something while I've gotten your attention.

210
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:15,160
I think you should consider coming over to our side.

211
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:16,020
Your side?

212
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:18,500
Sure, it's a lot of fun working with us.

213
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:19,700
My, how tempting.

214
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,180
Thank you, but I refuse.

215
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:25,640
I'm afraid I've sworn my absolute loyalty to the Wizard King.

216
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:27,160
Yes, of course you have.

217
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:28,900
Well, that's a terrible shame.

218
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:40,380
I figure that makes us about even.

219
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:43,620
You're right, it is a shame.

220
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:48,460
A shame that there were traitors hiding among the ranks of the Magic Knights.

221
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:57,800
Now then, one last thing.

222
00:16:58,700 --> 00:16:59,200
Uh-huh.

223
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:07,280
Whoever that is, go get rid of him!

224
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,460
Aaaaaah!

225
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:13,960
I didn't intend to involve myself.

226
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:16,460
I mean, maybe a little bit.

227
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:24,300
Guess we're done.

228
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:28,120
Splendid job, you two.

229
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:31,500
Not only did you discover the Magic Knight traitors and capture them,

230
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:33,860
but you managed to round up the entire bandit group.

231
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:37,440
To be fair, we found the boss man unconscious up in a tree.

232
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:40,940
Haha, sometimes things just work out.

233
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,880
But, with my deepest sincerity,

234
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:46,100
you both did well.

235
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:49,820
Yami, William,

236
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:52,500
I'm so impressed with your performance.

237
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:57,200
I'd like to invite you to be captains of two new Magic Knight squads.

238
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:58,380
You're kidding!

239
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,540
You're asking us to lead our own squads?

240
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:03,680
I hope that you'll accept.

241
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:11,320
So, if both of us made the captain spot at once, I guess it's a tie.

242
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:12,100
That's true.

243
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:14,080
But the real race lies ahead.

244
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:14,680
Uh-huh.

245
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:16,520
I'll win.

246
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:16,980
Watch.

247
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:17,800
Keep dreaming.

248
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:20,160
I have every confidence in you.

249
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:22,980
So, Yami, what kind of squad would you like to form?

250
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:24,260
What kind, huh?

251
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:25,720
How do I put it?

252
00:18:26,420 --> 00:18:27,220
Let me see.

253
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:31,180
How about a place for misfits to belong?

254
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:34,900
Where things like your rank and bloodline don't make any difference.

255
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:37,040
Where even hooligans are welcome.

256
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:39,960
You know, like the home you gave me.

257
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:40,680
I see.

258
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:42,160
An excellent idea.

259
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:45,180
As for the name, give me a second.

260
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:49,060
If I want lots of different people bringing all their colors to the table,

261
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:51,640
mixing them up till it's a big mess.

262
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:52,820
Hmm.

263
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:53,900
Oh.

264
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:56,780
If you put a bunch of different colors together, you'd get black.

265
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,360
So, I'll call us the Black, uh, the Black Bulls.

266
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:02,120
The Black Bulls it is.

267
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:03,060
Nice choice.

268
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:04,160
It suits you well.

269
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,340
And your team?

270
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:06,260
If I could.

271
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:08,460
I'd like to call mine the Golden Dawn.

272
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:09,520
Golden Dawn?

273
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:10,160
That's right.

274
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:14,080
And when it becomes the best of all, consider it my tribute to you.

275
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:18,580
True to its name, my squad will bring the shining gold of dawn to our world,

276
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:20,360
covering it with warmth and light.

277
00:19:21,220 --> 00:19:23,760
Just as sunlight pierces even the darkest night,

278
00:19:24,060 --> 00:19:27,340
we'll serve as a reminder to the people that Daybreak is sure to come.

279
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:29,680
You think really highly of yourself.

280
00:19:29,940 --> 00:19:31,220
Such a beautiful sentiment.

281
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:32,740
I'm expecting great things.

282
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:37,220
Starting today, I hereby name you the official captain of the Golden Dawn.

283
00:19:37,540 --> 00:19:39,020
Congratulations to you, William.

284
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:39,660
William, sir.

285
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:47,160
And Yami, from this moment on, you will be recognized as founder and leader of the Black Bulls.

286
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:48,880
Best of luck, Captain.

287
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:54,920
Let's do this, Goldie Guts.

288
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:01,640
And that's that.

289
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:04,740
Neat, huh?

290
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:08,340
Well, uh, a bunch of stuff did happen.

291
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:11,080
Um, what's the point you were trying to make again?

292
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:13,400
No, to never give up.

293
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:15,660
No matter how many times you may fall down.

294
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,480
Even if you're about to lose it all.

295
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:19,460
You can't quit on your dreams.

296
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:21,280
Always push past your limits.

297
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:23,780
So what if your rival outdid you this one time?

298
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:24,440
That's nothing.

299
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:27,400
If you lose 99 battles, just win the 100th.

300
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,480
Um, I'll keep that in mind.

301
00:20:29,940 --> 00:20:31,760
Could have said it from the start, though.

302
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:32,920
Ow!

303
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:35,180
Sorry, there was a great story.

304
00:20:35,260 --> 00:20:36,220
Please don't cross my head.

305
00:20:36,820 --> 00:20:39,420
You know, the captain said some smart stuff in there.

306
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:41,180
There's no reason to be sad.

307
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:42,320
All right.

308
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:45,420
Time to work hard, catch up to Yuno, and leave him behind.

309
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:47,620
Hey, that reminds me.

310
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:51,340
Isn't it about time we got back the results from the Royal Knight Selection Exam?

311
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:54,380
Uh, yeah, I think so.

312
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:54,720
Woo!

313
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:55,800
Can't wait to see.

314
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:58,680
Bring it on, Mr. Owl.

315
00:20:58,680 --> 00:20:59,520
I'm ready for you.

316
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:03,000
Damn.

317
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:05,060
That's the biggest owl I've ever heard.

318
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:10,180
Well, whoever you are, you can quit banging the door down already.

319
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:13,280
If you're looking for Captain Yami's black buzz, then you came to the...

320
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:16,320
Whoa, what just happened?

321
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:22,080
Hey, I recognize her.

322
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:24,180
That's Foigolian's sister!

323
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:27,500
What the hell says when you do this?

324
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:30,000
I'll be fine.

325
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:35,000
I'll be fine.

326
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:45,020
What's the winner?

327
00:21:45,020 --> 00:22:15,000
Thank you.

328
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:45,000
Thank you.

329
00:22:45,020 --> 00:22:47,020
Thank you.

330
00:23:15,020 --> 00:23:17,020
Thank you.

331
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:19,020
Thank you.

332
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:21,020
Thank you.

333
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:23,020
Thank you.

334
00:23:23,020 --> 00:23:24,520
I think you left some out.

335
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:25,980
We're on the mask Goldy Guts.

336
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:28,440
No, Baldy Guts Long John's Mustache Teacup.

337
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:29,540
Wait, no, damn it, I forgot.

338
00:23:29,660 --> 00:23:30,820
Just call me William.

339
00:23:32,020 --> 00:23:38,720
The selection exam results will be here any minute now.

340
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:39,680
I mean, not that it matters.

341
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:41,080
I totally made the cut, huh?

342
00:23:41,340 --> 00:23:42,020
What do you mean?

343
00:23:42,060 --> 00:23:43,060
I sound like I'm panicking.

344
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:44,980
Black Clover, page 87.

345
00:23:44,980 --> 00:23:46,760
Formation of the Royal Knights.

346
00:23:47,080 --> 00:23:48,540
I'm on fire, baby!

